        }
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "blk_n5j8wy1x7k",
          "type": "heading",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "text": "Websites as a commons",
            "level": "h1",
            "size": "display",
            "eyebrow": "About OpenSpace"
          },
          "column": 0,
          "variant": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "blk_ghvbae9rxf",
          "type": "text",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "content": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "attrs": {
                    "preset": "lead"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "OpenSpace is an open-source website builder with the polish of Squarespace and none of the lock-in. It's built in the open, and anyone can run their own copy."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "column": 1,
          "variant": "default"
        },
        {
          "id": "blk_d8w5bmxd6q",
          "type": "button",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "label": "View on GitHub",
            "link": {
              "type": "url",
              "url": "https://github.com/omniharmonic/openspace"
            },
            "role": "primary",
            "secondaryLabel": "Read the docs",
            "secondaryLink": {
              "type": "url",
              "url": "https://docs.openspace.dev"
            }
          },
          "column": 1,
          "variant": "default"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sec_5vmt0tewm4",
      "preset": "about/two-column-text@1",
      "label": "Heading with reading columns",
      "layout": {
        "mode": "stack",
        "columns": {
          "d": [
            12
          ]
        },
        "gap": "lg"
      },
      "style": {
        "colorTheme": "light"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "blk_f4anx1wkb4",
          "type": "heading",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "text": "Builders charge rent on commodities",
            "level": "h2",
            "size": "auto",
            "eyebrow": "Why we built it",
            "subheading": "Hosting, a CDN, an editor and AI help used to justify a monthly bill. Today they're free or open source. What was missing was the integration and the design quality."
          },
          "variant": "split"
        },
        {
          "id": "blk_h4zknahfpx",
          "type": "text",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "content": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A small nonprofit with a newsletter and a donate button can easily pay hundreds a year, indefinitely, for what is mostly static hosting and a form. Stop paying and the site disappears, along with the design work and the audience list."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "OpenSpace takes the other path. Every site is a normal project in its owner's GitHub account, built with Astro and served free. The editor renders the same components as the published site, so what you see is what visitors get, and the shared Hub only does what static sites can't: forms, newsletters, analytics, members and checkout."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The result is a website builder that costs the project almost nothing per site, which is what makes free forever a property of the design rather than a promotion."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "variant": "columns"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
